# MONITOR—Set Up Monitor Address -- override
# The manual's Operation is prose ("MONITOR sets up an address range for
# the monitor hardware using the content of EAX (RAX in 64-bit mode) as an
# effective address"). v1 has no monitor hardware (MWAIT returns at once,
# which the manual allows: "MWAIT ... may exit ... for any reason"), so
# MONITOR only checks the address as a read through DS (overridable) would:
# the faults are the manual's (#GP/#SS for the segment, #PF). ECX holds
# extensions, none defined: #GP(0) if ECX != 0.
@operation
IF ECX != 0 THEN #GP(0); FI;
IF AddressSize = 16 THEN a := AX; ELSE IF AddressSize = 32 THEN a := EAX; ELSE a := RAX; FI;
tmp := Memory8[DS:a];
